cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying article and, for the data, the Zenodo record."
type: software
title: "Unrest Index, tracker-derived travel distance and optical flow in broiler video: analysis code"
version: "2.2-revision"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived per-step time series for the article "Comparison of the
  Unrest Index with Tracker-Derived Travel Distance and Optical Flow in Broiler
  Videos" (Animals, manuscript animals-4688242, under review). The Unrest Index
  (Hausdorff distance between consecutive sets of bird positions) is compared
  with tracker-derived travel distance and dense optical flow on eight overhead
  recordings. The revision adds a controlled comparison of position read-outs
  (raw box centre, tracker box centre and mask area centroid of identical
  instances), a decomposition of model and read-out effects, a quantification of
  shared-coordinate agreement, and paired moving-block bootstrap intervals.
